        "Crus of clitoris",
        "Urethra",
        "Ischiocavernosus muscle"
      ],
      "createdAt": "2026-05-27T19:50:39.122Z",
      "subjectId": "anatomy",
      "difficulty": "exam",
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "The deep perineal pouch contains the external urethral sphincter, the membranous part of the urethra (in males) or a portion of the urethra (in females), and the deep transverse perineal muscles. The bulb of the penis, crus of the clitoris, and ischiocavernosus muscle are all components of the superficial perineal pouch.",
      "subjectTitle": "Anatomy"
    }
